    "q-11728": {
      "dom_id": "step-q11728",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)=5{e}^{x}+2{x}^{2}-3$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{e}^{x}+2{x}^{2}-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =5{e}^{x}+2(2x)-0 \\\\  & =5{e}^{x}+4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
