    "q-340277": {
      "dom_id": "step-q340277",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)=3\\cdot {4}^{x}-2{e}^{x}$, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\cdot {4}^{x}-2{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\cdot {4}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({4}^{x})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)\\cdot {4}^{x}-2{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)\\cdot {4}^{x}-2{e}^{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)\\cdot {4}^{1}-2{e}^{1} \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)-2e.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
