    "q-340284": {
      "dom_id": "step-q340284",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-3\\cdot {2}^{x}$, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-3\\cdot {2}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5))-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\cdot {2}^{x}) \\\\  & =0-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({2}^{x}) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\cdot {2}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\cdot {2}^{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\cdot {2}^{1} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
