    "q-340285": {
      "dom_id": "step-q340285",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)=5\\cdot {7}^{x}$, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\cdot {7}^{x}) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({7}^{x}) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\cdot {7}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\cdot {7}^{x})|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\cdot {7}^{0} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
